            "value": [
              {
                "dsDescriptionValue": {
                  "typeName": "dsDescriptionValue",
                  "multiple": false,
                  "typeClass": "primitive",
                  "value": "An overview of the experimental and simulation data based on the coronary arterial network of a single human heart as described in the listed paper. We provide data at three levels: the skeleton data, with connected voxels forming vascular segments and nodes and local estimates of vessel size (part 3), the representation as a graph in matlab (i.e. nodes and elements, or edges and vertices, part 4), and a range of excel files containing the source data for the various figures and tables, with also an explanation how to obtain such data from the matlab graph."
                },
